    "extracted text": "The synthesis procedure involves mixing germanium oxide (GeO2) and boric acid (H3BO3) dissolved in de-mineralized water with an aqueous solution of 6-azoniaspiro-[5,5]-undecane hydroxide (46.1 wt.%). The mixture was stirred and heated at 80°C to increase the solubility of germanium oxide. After cooling, tetraethylorthosilicate (TEOS) was added dropwise under vigorous stirring. The milky homogeneous mixture was charged in a rotating stainless-steel autoclave and heated at 170°C for 7 or 14 days. The solid product was collected by filtration, washed with de-mineralized water, dried overnight at 80°C and finally calcined at 550°C for 5 h. The H2O/SiO2 ratio was kept fixed at 30 for all syntheses.",
    
    "property mapping": "SiO2/GeO2 - Ratio of silicon to germanium sources, invert to get Ge/Si ratio\nSiO2/B2O3 - Ratio of silicon to boron sources, convert to get B/Si ratio\nNa/SiO2 - Ratio of sodium to silicon\nOH−/SiO2 - Ratio of hydroxide to silicon\nSDA/SiO2 - Ratio of structure directing agent to silicon\nt (days) - Crystallization time in days, convert to hours\nH2O/SiO2 = 30 - Water to silicon ratio (mentioned in table legend)\nCrystallization temperature = 170°C (mentioned in table legend)\nSDA = 6-azonia-spiro-[5,5]-undecane hydroxide (from extracted text)",
    
    "formula abbreviations": "SDA = Structure Directing Agent, specifically 6-azonia-spiro-[5,5]-undecane hydroxide\n∞ symbol in ratios means the component was not included in the synthesis\n– symbol in Na/SiO2 column means sodium was not added",
    
